# Written at run time by the hooks, the scripts and the status line. Keep them out of git: the logs
# record fragments of commands and of what was typed, the state directory holds session mail,
# compaction checkpoints and usage readings, and worktrees/ holds agent checkouts. No trailing slash
# on the first two, so the links the settings file asks Claude Code to make for them inside a
# worktree are ignored too. The four lines after /logs re-include the real logs directory (a link
# is not a directory to git, so it stays ignored), ignore its contents again, and re-include the
# two audit ledgers the expert-review skill tracks, so a plain `git add` takes them.
/state
/logs
!/logs/
/logs/*
!/logs/audit-runs.jsonl
!/logs/audit-findings.jsonl
/worktrees/
/settings.local.json
/skills/*/.roll.lock
/skills/*/.roll-staging-*/
